# Markdown table separator format

Applies to **all** Markdown tables in this project, in any file (docs, rules, README, etc.).

## Markdown tables inside Steps

Wide 3–4 column tables (Terraform variables, etc.) **must** be wrapped so narrow viewports scroll horizontally instead of crushing columns (letters stacking vertically):

```mdx
<div class="wide-table-wrap">

| Variable | Default | Required | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | ----- |
| `vpc_id` | — | yes | VPC for mount targets |

</div>
```

Styles live in `src/styles/splash-overrides.css` (`.wide-table-wrap`). Keep blank lines inside the div so Markdown still parses the table.

## Rule

Table separator rows **must** have a space between each pipe (`|`) and the dashes. No exceptions.

```markdown
❌ Wrong (no spaces — will be flagged)
|-----------|-----------|-------|

✅ Correct (space between | and dashes — required)
| --------- | --------- | ----- |
```

When creating or editing a table, always use the spaced separator row. Fix any existing tables that use the wrong format.
